messages.content:
A tiny bakery website

Screens of this mockup, as a tree:
@home: the first screen of A tiny bakery website (this screen)
  @bread-shelf: Bread section of a bakery website on a phone, with sourdough, rye and baguette listed with prices
    @rye-details: Detail page for a rye bread loaf at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients and add-to-cart button (not made yet)
    @baguette-details: Detail page for a baguette at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients and add-to-cart button (not made yet)
  @my-account: Account screen of a bakery website on a phone with order history and saved pickup slots
  @pastry-case: Pastry section of a bakery website on a phone, with croissants, danish and eclairs listed with prices
    @croissant-details: The croissant details screen, opened by "Details" (not made yet)
    @danish-details: The danish details screen, opened by "Details" (not made yet)
    @eclair-details: The eclair details screen, opened by "Details" (not made yet)
  @cake-orders: Custom cake order form for a bakery website on a phone (not made yet)
  @sourdough-details: Detail page for a sourdough loaf at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients, ferment time and add-to-cart button (not made yet)
  @berry-tart-details: Detail page for a berry tart at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients, allergens and add-to-cart button (not made yet)
  @cart: Cart screen of a bakery website on a phone, with cinnamon knots and a sourdough loaf, totals and a checkout button (not made yet)

Design it for a phone screen, at most 390 px wide.

The screen as it is now:
<title>Bakery home</title>
<meta name="idea" content="Bakery as a sectioned product catalogue with a daily bake-slot calendar and a sticky bottom order bar">
<p><small>Freshly baked, daily</small></p>
<h1>Maple Crumb Bakery</h1>
<nav style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.5rem">
<button data-action="@bread-shelf: Bread section of a bakery website on a phone, with sourdough, rye and baguette listed with prices">Bread</button>
<button data-action="@pastry-case: Pastry section of a bakery website on a phone, with croissants, danish and eclairs listed with prices">Pastries</button>
<button data-action="@cake-orders: Custom cake order form for a bakery website on a phone">Cakes</button>
</nav>
<h3>Today's bake times</h3>
<label>Pickup slot
<select id="slot">
<option>8:00 AM</option>
<option>11:30 AM</option>
<option>3:00 PM</option>
</select>
</label>
<article>
<h3>Cinnamon knot</h3>
<p>Brown butter glaze, baked at dawn</p>
<p><mark id="knotPrice">$3.50</mark></p>
<label>Qty <input id="qty" type="number" min="0" value="0" style="width:5rem"></label>
<p><small>Subtotal: <strong id="subtotal">$0.00</strong></small></p>
</article>
<article>
<h3>Sourdough loaf</h3>
<p>72-hour ferment, crackly crust</p>
<p><strong>$7.00</strong></p>
<button data-action="@sourdough-details: Detail page for a sourdough loaf at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients, ferment time and add-to-cart button">View details</button>
</article>
<article>
<h3>Berry tart</h3>
<p>Seasonal berries, almond cream</p>
<p><strong>$5.25</strong></p>
<button data-action="@berry-tart-details: Detail page for a berry tart at a bakery website on a phone, with ingredients, allergens and add-to-cart button">View details</button>
</article>
<footer style="position:sticky;bottom:0">
<button data-action="@cart: Cart screen of a bakery website on a phone, with cinnamon knots and a sourdough loaf, totals and a checkout button">Cart (<span id="count">0</span>)</button>
<button data-action="@my-account: Account screen of a bakery website on a phone with order history and saved pickup slots">Account</button>
</footer>
<script>
const price=3.5;
const qty=document.getElementById('qty');
const sub=document.getElementById('subtotal');
const count=document.getElementById('count');
function update(){
const n=Math.max(0,parseInt(qty.value)||0);
sub.textContent='$'+(n*price).toFixed(2);
count.textContent=n;
}
qty.addEventListener('input',update);
update();
</script>

Reply with this screen again, changed only as follows; keep everything else as it is, including its data-action links, and add no second control for a screen it already links to: Make the main heading say "Fresh bread daily"

